01:15:08,340 --> 01:15:10,370
It rained outside.

1832
01:15:11,170 --> 01:15:12,740
Only Ju Bin knew that it rained overnight.

1833
01:15:12,740 --> 01:15:13,740
She went for a walk.

1834
01:15:13,740 --> 01:15:14,840
- Right.
- Really?

1835
01:15:16,770 --> 01:15:18,670
I never got a chance to look around.

1836
01:15:18,670 --> 01:15:20,040
(An hour ago)

1837
01:15:20,900 --> 01:15:23,040
When would I ever come to a place like this again?

1838
01:15:28,500 --> 01:15:34,400
(Canada's vast wilderness unfolds everywhere she sees.)

1839
01:15:38,300 --> 01:15:40,240
I feel so free.

1840
01:15:40,240 --> 01:15:43,300
(Following the vast landscape, one's mind feels free for a moment.)

1841
01:15:43,570 --> 01:15:46,400
I've always wanted to come here before my death.

1842
01:15:52,270 --> 01:15:55,040
It's a dead end. I feel like I can go through.

1843
01:15:55,940 --> 01:15:57,040
- But I'm worried...
- Yes?

1844
01:15:58,340 --> 01:16:00,170
I'll meet an actual bear.

1845
01:16:01,370 --> 01:16:03,940
(She rushes back home in case she runs into a bear.)

1846
01:16:04,840 --> 01:16:06,770
It was a field like I've never seen before.

1847
01:16:07,370 --> 01:16:08,640
You might run into a bear.

1848
01:16:08,700 --> 01:16:09,970
- Weren't you scared?
- No.

1849
01:16:10,940 --> 01:16:12,970
It was really bright.

1850
01:16:12,970 --> 01:16:14,040
You really are fearless.

1851
01:16:15,040 --> 01:16:17,200
It's not that scary out there.

1852
01:16:17,340 --> 01:16:18,770
I've watched too many YouTube videos.

1853
01:16:18,940 --> 01:16:20,670
I won't know what to do if I spot a bear.

1854
01:16:21,400 --> 01:16:22,670
You should check it out.

1855
01:16:22,870 --> 01:16:24,340
I can't go there.

1856
01:16:24,570 --> 01:16:26,400
(He's being serious.)

1857
01:16:26,610 --> 01:16:27,640
No.

1858
01:16:28,110 --> 01:16:31,170
(I'll just stick to eating.)

1859
01:16:33,110 --> 01:16:34,300
I'm full now.

1860
01:16:34,770 --> 01:16:36,110
That was such a good meal.

1861
01:16:36,110 --> 01:16:37,970
(Travel itinerary available on our official social media account)

1862
01:16:37,970 --> 01:16:40,000
(Alberta, Canada, the third episode)

1863
01:16:40,000 --> 01:16:43,740
(It's not over yet!)

1864
01:16:43,800 --> 01:16:46,800
